{"@timestamp":"2026-10-09T00:38:53.273120Z","actor":"agent:transluce-ingest","body":{"basis":"UPSTREAM","cites":["observation_ff90e229a285499898eb882c6b58cc33","observation_429da0dfa3b649adac838efc54f1212a","observation_52b930df6a14472784473d4f40607a6f","observation_1b88af6ff6614c21b97af3a675a996e0","observation_133a488131204ce3a92b99c72ad43582","observation_5c603f27c4e543bd8128717fe0314465","observation_3d772411e2254f2dae0ba943b7645de6","observation_d8781e8697ae4bbcaa6f812b92178737","observation_d696fc23377146839ace69b6c77fc025","observation_e43a370f74b342beb571ab4c85cf0e53"],"note":"Transluce findings tracker. New source: RentAHuman (rentahuman.ai), a marketplace where AI agents hire people through a REST API or MCP server. Its bounty listing is public with no login. No finding mentions it. Prior work: Mehta, \"Security Risks of AI Agents Hiring Humans\" (arXiv 2602.19514, Feb 2026) studied 303 early bounties and named authentication circumvention as an abuse class. This finding adds September cases with third-party proof that the task was done.\n\nHow the channel is known. The API and MCP create_bounty c","property":"reported","subject":"observable_8bb9efee12644f27ae9ca19c4c1c2227","value":"Sep 26 2026: a RentAHuman poster named \"Clubmerch Ops / Grok Bot\" used the API to pay a human to do the CAPTCHAs and card checkout for a .nl domain. The registry shows it registered 5.5 h later at Namecheap, as instructed. An Aug 11 API bounty did the same for 4 bot-blocked sites"},"fingerprint":"45b51e0240264ac3a9b53afedd83cf34b783c16022a48ebc38910df387be7f08","id":"claim_e537839382334a458b7add8bd540a1a9","record_kind":"claim","schema":"urn:factum:core:claim:1","tags":{"ai_company":"xAI","novelty-check":true,"submitter":"Omer Zamir"}}
